WEBVTT

00:04.210 --> 00:09.100
Final exams start next week, so put 
your pedals to the metal this week.

00:09.100 --> 00:10.520
Ugh...

00:10.520 --> 00:13.660
No, not "ugh." All right, you're excused.

00:15.050 --> 00:18.340
<i>I've already gone over all 
of the subjects on the tests,</i>

00:18.340 --> 00:20.350
<i>so now if I just review the tough parts—</i>

00:20.350 --> 00:21.520
Ugh!

00:22.570 --> 00:26.420
It feels like midterms just 
ended and now finals already?

00:26.740 --> 00:28.720
Do you hate tests that much, Fuyuki-san?

00:28.720 --> 00:31.000
There ain't nothing to like about them!

00:31.320 --> 00:34.180
But if you're asking, Tsubasa, 
does that mean you do like them?

00:34.630 --> 00:36.980
Well, not "like" so much,

00:37.350 --> 00:40.250
but in the sense that you get to 
directly see your efforts pay off,

00:40.250 --> 00:42.100
I guess they are satisfying in a way.

00:42.100 --> 00:45.860
Huh? I've never heard anyone 
talk about tests like that.

00:45.860 --> 00:49.650
Uh, sorry. I know I sound boring.

00:49.650 --> 00:54.330
No, no, the opposite! 
That's my Tsuba-cha. Good for you.

00:54.530 --> 00:57.120
Huh? Well, I wasn't trying to—

00:57.120 --> 01:00.190
Okay, I'm starting to get motivated!

01:00.190 --> 01:02.120
Tsubasa, Tsubasa, are you free later?

01:02.120 --> 01:03.710
Huh? Yeah.

01:03.710 --> 01:05.460
Wanna have a study party at my place?

01:06.680 --> 01:07.320
Um.

01:08.440 --> 01:09.240
Mm-hmm.

01:22.140 --> 01:24.810
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

01:25.650 --> 01:29.020
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

02:37.180 --> 02:39.930
Super Cute Angels ♥

02:37.180 --> 02:39.930
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are</b>

02:37.180 --> 02:39.930
<b>Boom!</b>

02:37.180 --> 02:39.930
<b>Super Adorable</b>

02:40.800 --> 02:44.930
<b>Episode 6:
Natsukawa-Senpai Is Super Good-Looking</b>

02:40.800 --> 02:44.930
<b>Episode 6:
Natsukawa-Senpai Is Super Good-Looking</b>

02:43.240 --> 02:45.350
So why do I have to go, too?

02:45.590 --> 02:47.980
More people means more fun!

02:49.040 --> 02:51.110
You really don't plan to study, do you?

02:51.110 --> 02:56.970
Of course I do! I'm actually 
pretty worried about this one.

02:56.970 --> 03:01.120
Well, having Shiki there should help. 
He seems pretty smart.

03:01.120 --> 03:05.030
Tsubasa is like our very own private tutor!

03:05.750 --> 03:07.370
Private tutor?

03:08.350 --> 03:12.800
<i>I guess teaching people will 
help me learn, too, so why not.</i>

03:13.030 --> 03:14.250
I'm home.

03:14.250 --> 03:14.980
Excuse us.

03:14.980 --> 03:16.330
'Scuse us.

03:16.330 --> 03:17.680
Is everybody gone?

03:17.680 --> 03:22.410
Yeah. Mom and Dad are at work and 
my little sister is at dance class.

03:22.410 --> 03:24.520
Huh? You have a little sister?

03:24.520 --> 03:27.810
I sure do! Don't I totally 
fit the big sis role?

03:28.080 --> 03:30.400
No way. You're way more the little sis type.

03:30.400 --> 03:32.070
Aww.

03:32.290 --> 03:36.650
I'll get something to drink, 
so go ahead and wait in my room.

03:36.650 --> 03:37.920
Second floor, okay?

03:37.920 --> 03:39.560
Fine, but which room?

03:39.560 --> 03:41.360
The one way in the back.

03:41.360 --> 03:42.520
Okay.

03:44.820 --> 03:49.080
We've never come to Fuyuki's house before. 
How would we know if she doesn't tell us?

03:49.080 --> 03:52.880
Oh. Actually, I came over to hang out once.

03:52.880 --> 03:54.050
Huh?!

03:54.050 --> 03:57.970
But we stayed in the living room 
and just watched a movie together.

03:57.970 --> 03:59.690
I've never seen her bedroom.

04:01.720 --> 04:03.530
So, Shiki, you're like...

04:03.960 --> 04:05.310
a sneaky pervert.

04:05.310 --> 04:09.200
Perv—! No! Nothing even happened!

04:09.200 --> 04:12.240
Fuyuki-san even fell asleep part way through.

04:12.240 --> 04:13.510
Yeah, right.

04:14.330 --> 04:15.530
This room?

04:24.020 --> 04:25.750
This is totally like Fuyuki.

04:25.750 --> 04:26.750
No kidding.

04:36.740 --> 04:39.570
<i>I've never been in a girl's room before.</i>

04:39.570 --> 04:41.850
<i>It smells really good!</i>

04:43.630 --> 04:47.330
<i>I guess because Fuyuki-san 
spends every day in here.</i>

04:47.790 --> 04:49.520
<i>Playing, sleeping...</i>

04:55.270 --> 04:56.590
<i>changing.</i>

04:57.400 --> 05:00.030
<i>Wait, what am I thinking?!</i>

05:03.730 --> 05:05.270
A blatant pervert.

05:06.110 --> 05:09.800
Thanks for waiting. I brought some pop!

05:15.090 --> 05:17.200
Good choice. I love this stuff.

05:17.200 --> 05:20.120
It's so good, right? I love it, too.

05:20.120 --> 05:22.050
Ribbon Napolin?

05:25.050 --> 05:29.190
Oh, you've never had it before? 
'Kay, lemme know what you think.

05:29.190 --> 05:30.270
Thanks.

05:30.970 --> 05:31.480
Thank you.

05:39.460 --> 05:40.700
This is really good!

05:40.700 --> 05:45.460
Right? It's been around for forever. 
It's the soul drink of Hokkaido.

05:45.460 --> 05:46.660
Huh...

05:47.720 --> 05:51.080
I love the bubbles! It really clears the head.

05:51.080 --> 05:55.210
That makes sense. It's the 
perfect soda for a study party!

05:56.320 --> 05:57.160
Definitely.

05:57.160 --> 05:59.960
Oh, right! Why don't we quiz each other?

05:59.960 --> 06:02.340
Fine with me, but on what subject?

06:02.690 --> 06:05.480
We should do one that'll be 
on the first day of tests.

06:05.480 --> 06:06.760
How about world history?

06:06.760 --> 06:08.150
Okay!

06:08.150 --> 06:09.890
M'kay, Tsubasa first!

06:09.890 --> 06:11.890
<b>Revised
World History {世界史}</b>

06:11.890 --> 06:15.120
Okay, then. I'll start with something simple.

06:15.630 --> 06:20.420
The belief that God's will is absolute 
and that any one individual's salvation

06:17.900 --> 06:28.410
Calvin and the Reformation in Switzerland
A few years after Luther, the Reformation began in Switzerland as well.
It was led by Zwingli, who had been greatly influenced by Erasmus
and Luther and rose up during the church reforms in Zürich to stand
against the Lutherans. He later died in war, fighting against the Catholics.
 One figure who rose to take his place was Jean Calvin.*

 *Jean Calvin
 July 10, 1509 - May 27, 1564
 A 16th Century theologian and church reformist.
One of the leading figures in the Protestant Reformation.

 Born in Picardy, France. Calvin's beliefs and teachings
are said to have become the foundation of the denomination
known as Calvinism.

06:20.420 --> 06:23.420
has already been determined in advance by God

06:23.420 --> 06:26.910
is a Christian theological 
doctrine advanced by Calvin.

06:26.910 --> 06:28.410
What is that doctrine called?

06:28.410 --> 06:30.970
Uh, what was it...

06:30.970 --> 06:32.800
A hint. A place you go to is called...?

06:33.710 --> 06:35.940
Ah, a destination! Predestination!

06:35.940 --> 06:37.360
Correct, Akino-san!

06:38.160 --> 06:42.050
Right! You can't go somewhere 
without a destination!

06:42.050 --> 06:43.880
You're up next, Sayurin!

06:43.880 --> 06:46.260
Um, okay. In that case...

06:47.000 --> 06:52.560
In England in 1559, queen of the House of 
Tudor, Elizabeth the First, passed an act

06:52.560 --> 06:56.540
prescribing standards for worship 
and prayer in the Church of England.

06:56.540 --> 06:57.530
What was it called?

06:58.430 --> 07:00.060
The Act of Uniformity.

07:00.810 --> 07:03.330
Of course you knew that right away.

07:03.330 --> 07:05.840
Okay, the next question is yours, Fuyuki.

07:05.840 --> 07:08.970
Huh?! Um...

07:12.420 --> 07:17.640
I hear that in the old days, Kitami produced 
70 percent of the whole world's mint!

07:17.640 --> 07:19.070
What are you talking about?!

07:19.410 --> 07:21.610
That is pretty impressive, though.

07:21.610 --> 07:25.260
Oh, no kidding! No wonder my grandma 
always has mint candies at her house!

07:25.260 --> 07:30.140
Dad just told me about it! 
Crazy, huh? So wild, right?

07:30.500 --> 07:33.780
Sure it's wild, but it has nothing 
to do with the test subjects.

07:33.780 --> 07:35.520
It isn't even a real question.

07:37.010 --> 07:39.920
I was trying to impress you guys.

07:39.920 --> 07:43.780
Let's work together, Fuyuki-san. 
It isn't too late yet.

07:43.780 --> 07:44.970
You can do it if you try!

07:44.970 --> 07:46.870
Tsuba-cha!

07:46.870 --> 07:49.620
Okay, I'm gonna work super hard!

07:49.620 --> 07:51.870
You sure are easy on her, Shiki.

07:52.270 --> 07:54.400
You'd better not forget to teach me, too!

07:54.400 --> 07:58.620
Of course not! 
Okay, here's the next question.

08:13.380 --> 08:16.020
Perhaps we'll have tatsuta fried 
chicken for tonight's meal.

08:21.840 --> 08:26.600
I haven't studied this hard in a thousand 
years! My head is all wack now!

08:26.600 --> 08:27.630
I'm exhausted.

08:27.630 --> 08:30.550
You both worked really hard. I'm impressed.

08:31.090 --> 08:32.700
What time is it anyway?

08:33.720 --> 08:36.180
Oh, crap! It's past my curfew!

08:36.180 --> 08:38.710
I was concentrating so hard, 
I lost track of time!

08:38.710 --> 08:41.150
Sorry! I've gotta go!

08:41.150 --> 08:43.130
Huh? Hold on, Tsubasa.

08:43.130 --> 08:44.260
Hey! Shiki!

08:44.260 --> 08:45.620
See you guys later!

08:50.620 --> 08:52.220
Thanks for having me over!

08:52.450 --> 08:54.000
I'm home!

09:03.810 --> 09:05.320
Tsuba-chi?

09:09.280 --> 09:12.910
Oh, okay. So you came over to study.

09:12.910 --> 09:16.660
Yes. Thank you so much for everything.

09:17.290 --> 09:20.210
<i>The sweet smell and soft feeling 
on my face haven't gone away.</i>

09:20.540 --> 09:24.740
All good, all good! Perfect timing 
since I just got home anyway.

09:24.740 --> 09:28.240
And you live really close. 
It's no trouble at all to drop you off.

09:28.240 --> 09:29.740
Thank you very much.

09:30.130 --> 09:32.760
By the way, Mii told me about you.

09:33.680 --> 09:35.830
That you're really good at piano.

09:36.850 --> 09:39.770
I've been practicing since I was little.

09:39.770 --> 09:42.130
Have you really?

09:43.830 --> 09:47.010
You might have already heard about this,

09:47.360 --> 09:51.280
but that girl had a rough 
Valentine's Day and got really depressed.

09:51.630 --> 09:55.690
I was worried how she'd be 
doing when she got home.

09:56.670 --> 09:58.630
But she came back all smiles!

09:58.630 --> 10:02.010
And couldn't stop talking about 
how good you are at piano!

10:02.010 --> 10:04.770
I thought it was so hilarious!

10:05.190 --> 10:08.890
<i>This is super embarrassing. 
My face feels so hot!</i>

10:09.440 --> 10:11.790
And it was a massive relief.

10:13.390 --> 10:15.510
So thank you, Tsuba-chi.

10:18.480 --> 10:19.710
My pleasure.

10:28.750 --> 10:32.760
Wow! Your house really is like a castle!

10:32.760 --> 10:33.760
Oh, not really.

10:34.330 --> 10:36.620
Thank you again very much for the ride.

10:36.620 --> 10:38.200
Oh, hold on.

10:38.200 --> 10:42.110
I bought this for myself, 
but I'll give it to you.

10:42.110 --> 10:43.160
It's cold!

10:43.160 --> 10:47.170
You're always working so hard, 
so that's a treat from Mama.

10:50.590 --> 10:52.210
Drink up and hang in there!

10:52.490 --> 10:54.090
M'kay bye!

10:56.350 --> 10:57.760
I will do my best!

10:57.760 --> 10:59.110
Tsubasa-chan!

11:04.100 --> 11:06.530
Exactly what time to do you think it is?!

11:14.340 --> 11:15.240
Tsubasa-chan.

11:16.120 --> 11:16.740
Yes?

11:17.680 --> 11:21.520
Would you mind throwing the burnable 
garbage out on your way to school?

11:21.520 --> 11:23.610
Certainly, Grandma.

11:27.450 --> 11:28.570
See you later.

11:33.550 --> 11:36.710
<i>Grandma really put me through 
the wringer last night.</i>

11:36.710 --> 11:39.140
<i>I'm still stressed out from that.</i>

11:39.610 --> 11:48.310
<b>Enjoy
Tea</b>

11:40.410 --> 11:44.470
As long as you are in this house, 
you will follow my rules.

11:44.470 --> 11:48.310
I have told you repeatedly that this 
is the condition for you staying here.

11:49.130 --> 11:51.570
Yes, that is absolutely right.

11:54.270 --> 11:57.250
I will put this incident aside for now.

11:57.250 --> 12:00.990
However, if you make another 
misstep like this again,

12:02.740 --> 12:04.750
you know what will happen.

12:04.750 --> 12:05.680
Yes.

12:06.280 --> 12:07.830
I truly am very sorry!

12:27.610 --> 12:29.180
<i>Is she from overseas?</i>

12:30.350 --> 12:32.510
<i>She looks so pretty.</i>

12:33.150 --> 12:36.070
<i>And so refined. Her beauty 
complements the snowy landscape.</i>

12:36.760 --> 12:38.980
<i>But what is she doing by the garbage?</i>

12:40.030 --> 12:42.810
<i>It doesn't look like 
she's carrying any trash.</i>

12:54.020 --> 12:56.160
They weren't nearly as 
intimidating as they sounded.

13:04.600 --> 13:11.350
Trash Station {ゴミステーション}

13:05.990 --> 13:08.730
Now that I've driven the riffraff away,

13:08.730 --> 13:11.350
please feel free to throw 
away all the trash you like.

13:11.350 --> 13:13.190
Huh? All right.

13:13.190 --> 13:15.860
And on that note, I shall now abscond.

13:17.570 --> 13:19.120
Ab-Abscond?

13:23.820 --> 13:26.700
Oh? Don't you mean Rena-senpai?

13:26.700 --> 13:27.910
Rena-senpai?

13:27.910 --> 13:31.480
White-pink hair in a short cut 
and a Japanese-style hairband?

13:31.480 --> 13:33.530
That's totally Rena-senpai!

13:33.920 --> 13:37.090
I'm so jealous you got to see 
her first thing in the morning!

13:37.360 --> 13:38.900
Do you know her, Fuyuki-san?

13:38.900 --> 13:41.880
I way more than know her. I adore her!

13:42.580 --> 13:45.480
She's won our beauty contest 
two years in a row.

13:45.480 --> 13:48.650
I think she has a parent 
or something from overseas.

13:48.650 --> 13:51.910
She's famous around here. A supreme beauty!

14:02.510 --> 14:04.420
Isn't she great?

14:04.420 --> 14:08.390
If I'm ever reborn, I wanna be 
reincarnated as a gyaru like her!

14:08.390 --> 14:09.600
Huh...

14:10.190 --> 14:13.920
<i>Well, she was pretty in an 
impossibly un-Japanese way.</i>

14:13.920 --> 14:15.850
Hey, Tsubasa!

14:16.460 --> 14:20.520
Wanna come over for another study 
party today? We can invite Sayuri, too!

14:20.520 --> 14:22.250
Ah, sorry.

14:22.250 --> 14:26.050
Starting today, I have to study 
alone until tests are over.

14:27.140 --> 14:31.020
Ah, but that doesn't mean I don't 
want to study with you guys!

14:31.020 --> 14:33.600
I just need to be alone to concentrate.

14:34.200 --> 14:38.810
Really? That's a bummer. But oh well.

14:40.170 --> 14:42.970
<i>I can't tell her how mad Grandma got.</i>

14:43.390 --> 14:45.820
<i>I don't want either of 
them to worry about me.</i>

14:45.820 --> 14:49.840
M'kay, I'll invite Sayurin and 
the two of us can study together!

14:49.840 --> 14:51.540
I have to turn you down, too.

14:51.540 --> 14:55.000
Sayurin? Wait, you're turning me down?!

14:55.000 --> 14:59.590
We'd end up talking and not studying, 
just like yesterday after Shiki left.

14:59.590 --> 15:01.520
Ugh, you're right.

15:01.870 --> 15:05.170
<i>So they didn't keep studying after I left?</i>

15:11.470 --> 15:14.090
Sayurin! Let's eat together.

15:14.090 --> 15:16.790
No way. I'm researching game strategies.

15:16.790 --> 15:18.490
Oh?

15:18.490 --> 15:21.040
Well, as long as I'm not bothering you.

15:21.040 --> 15:22.940
How much attention do you need anyway?

15:22.940 --> 15:26.190
But lunch isn't something you eat alone!

15:26.190 --> 15:28.150
And I just realized Tsubasa is gone.

15:28.150 --> 15:30.630
Hmm. No kidding.

15:31.300 --> 15:32.830
I wonder where he went.

15:33.120 --> 15:35.110
Right? Who does he think he is?

15:35.110 --> 15:39.060
Ahh. Sounds like you're mad at 
him for skipping the study party.

15:39.060 --> 15:44.090
N-No I'm not! I wouldn't get 
grouchy over such a little thing.

15:44.340 --> 15:48.340
Well, I'm sure he has a lot on his mind. 
Try not to worry about it.

15:51.370 --> 15:54.120
Sayurin, you sure sound 
like a nice old lady.

15:54.120 --> 15:56.580
There's no way you meant 
that as a compliment!

15:58.690 --> 16:01.690
<b>Library</b>

16:02.720 --> 16:05.750
<i>I decided to try out the 
library for a change of pace.</i>

16:05.750 --> 16:08.120
<i>It's so easy to study here. 
I'm getting a lot done.</i>

16:10.060 --> 16:11.010
<i>Is someone snoring?</i>

16:17.120 --> 16:18.660
<i>Rena-senpai?!</i>

16:19.120 --> 16:21.560
<i>She totally dozed off </i>here<i>?</i>

16:21.560 --> 16:24.490
<i>Forget about that. 
She looks so beautiful asleep!</i>

16:24.490 --> 16:27.250
<i>What could she be dreaming about 
to be so beautiful?!</i>

16:27.760 --> 16:31.520
<i>Ah, even just looking at her relaxes me.</i>

16:31.520 --> 16:34.670
<i>This is the perfect antidote for 
the stress of test studying!</i>

16:38.020 --> 16:38.890
<i>Is she awake?</i>

16:41.050 --> 16:42.940
But what about Sekigahara?

16:42.940 --> 16:44.540
<i>She's dreaming about war?!</i>

16:44.540 --> 16:46.940
<i>Dreaming about a bloodbath 
makes her smile like that?!</i>

16:50.490 --> 16:52.250
<i>She looked straight at me!</i>

16:52.250 --> 16:54.490
<i>Did she realize I'd been staring at her?</i>

16:54.490 --> 17:00.020
<i>Wait, wait. Try to focus, man. 
I'm not getting anything done.</i>

17:00.020 --> 17:02.220
<i>Okay. Study, study!</i>

17:07.010 --> 17:08.910
Wh-What is it?

17:09.930 --> 17:11.760
I'm on the library committee.

17:12.720 --> 17:15.910
As such, at this moment, 
I have authority over the library.

17:16.900 --> 17:17.560
I see.

17:17.770 --> 17:21.940
Essentially, as long as I approve, 
it is perfectly fine to sleep in here!

17:22.230 --> 17:24.100
<i>She's worried that I caught her sleeping!</i>

17:24.100 --> 17:26.980
Yeah, I actually don't mind at all.

17:26.980 --> 17:28.230
You have

17:28.230 --> 17:32.830
absolutely wonderful posture! 
Do you work out?

17:35.870 --> 17:39.120
Oh, that's right. 
You were studying. I'm so sorry!

17:39.120 --> 17:40.730
No, it's fine.

17:42.450 --> 17:45.900
This answer is marked as correct 
but is actually incorrect.

17:46.590 --> 17:47.280
Oh.

17:50.020 --> 17:51.090
You're right.

17:51.360 --> 17:55.900
If that's what you're being tested on, 
you must be a first-year student.

17:55.900 --> 17:57.690
Good luck with your studies!

17:57.690 --> 18:00.350
Uh, yeah. Thank you very much.

18:02.840 --> 18:07.290
<i>You mean she figured it out in 
her head after just one glance?</i>

18:09.940 --> 18:12.400
<i>Nah, there's no way she could do that.</i>

18:12.860 --> 18:15.830
<i>Maybe she used the same workbook before.</i>

18:20.400 --> 18:21.550
I'm home.

18:23.800 --> 18:25.050
Grandma?

18:26.190 --> 18:27.840
Welcome back.

18:28.920 --> 18:30.620
Uh, what's wrong?

18:30.620 --> 18:33.720
I have been thinking 
about something all day.

18:33.720 --> 18:37.480
About what I can possibly do 
to support you, Tsubasa-chan.

18:37.480 --> 18:38.180
Huh?

18:38.720 --> 18:42.150
I do realize that you are at a certain age

18:42.150 --> 18:45.100
where you may be facing issues 
that I cannot understand.

18:45.490 --> 18:46.950
Grandma...

18:46.950 --> 18:52.950
Nonetheless, since arriving in Hokkaido, 
you have clearly dropped your guard.

18:52.950 --> 18:58.090
What you need right now is time 
to develop your mental fortitude.

18:58.440 --> 18:59.240
In other words,

19:00.920 --> 19:02.370
the tea ceremony.

19:02.370 --> 19:15.250
<b>Enjoy
Tea</b>

19:02.770 --> 19:05.620
The tea ceremony will help 
eliminate your carnal desires.

19:06.020 --> 19:10.160
We often held tea lessons 
when you were in Tokyo,

19:10.160 --> 19:12.720
but this will be your first 
time since coming to Hokkaido.

19:13.190 --> 19:15.260
Is your technique perhaps waning?

19:15.960 --> 19:18.160
It is the same as learning to ride a bicycle.

19:18.160 --> 19:21.100
The body does not easily forget 
movements once memorized.

19:22.360 --> 19:23.470
Acceptable.

19:24.280 --> 19:25.410
Well, then...

19:27.480 --> 19:28.680
Who could that be?

19:28.680 --> 19:30.260
We will have to start over again.

19:30.260 --> 19:32.440
Tsubasa-chan, please answer that.

19:34.590 --> 19:37.990
I'm Natsukawa from next door. 
I've brought the neighborhood bulletin—

19:37.030 --> 19:38.630
Huh? Senpai?

19:39.630 --> 19:43.380
Neighborhood bulletin... 
so we're next-door neighbors?

19:43.380 --> 19:45.210
It's very nice to meet you again.

19:46.950 --> 19:49.870
I apologize for the delayed 
introduction. My name is Shiki—

19:49.170 --> 19:50.540
Japanese clothes!

19:53.360 --> 19:55.310
Outrageous!

19:56.020 --> 19:56.590
Huh?

20:00.720 --> 20:01.800
Huh?!

20:03.840 --> 20:10.600
<b>Enjoy
Tea</b>

20:05.350 --> 20:08.080
He is rather late. I wonder what happened.

20:11.140 --> 20:13.130
Tsubasa-chan, who is it?

20:29.480 --> 20:34.210
<i>Wh-Wh-What is even happening to me?!</i>

20:34.210 --> 20:36.730
Tsubasa! What do you think you are doing?!

20:36.730 --> 20:39.560
No, you're wrong! 
It isn't what it looks like!

20:41.090 --> 20:43.430
I dearly beg your pardon.

20:43.430 --> 20:48.680
I clumsily slipped, but the gentleman was 
kind enough to catch me from falling.

20:49.280 --> 20:51.100
Thank you very much.

20:56.180 --> 20:57.860
Here is the neighborhood bulletin.

20:58.370 --> 20:59.490
Oh, right.

21:00.260 --> 21:01.110
<i>Huh?</i>

21:01.110 --> 21:03.870
<i>She's suddenly acting totally different.</i>

21:04.330 --> 21:05.950
Oh, is that what happened?

21:05.950 --> 21:08.910
In that case, I do apologize 
for the unsightly display.

21:08.910 --> 21:11.720
Thank you for bringing the bulletin.

21:11.720 --> 21:13.870
Please take care on your way home.

21:14.400 --> 21:16.270
Well then, please excuse me.

21:21.190 --> 21:24.250
Since she brought the bulletin, 
does that mean she lives next door?

21:24.250 --> 21:26.930
Huh? Oh, yeah. It sounds like it.

21:26.930 --> 21:31.260
The master of the household always brings 
it over, so I've never seen her before.

21:31.690 --> 21:33.830
She is quite a lovely girl.

21:35.170 --> 21:37.960
<i>Grandma doesn't usually say things like that.</i>

21:43.990 --> 21:46.770
Well, Tsubasa-chan, let us return.

21:49.930 --> 21:50.630
Tsubasa!

21:50.630 --> 21:53.760
Ah, yes! Back to the tea ceremony!

21:53.760 --> 21:55.360
Enough tea for now.

21:55.360 --> 21:56.020
Huh?

21:58.000 --> 22:01.890
I can clearly see the reason 
you have let your guard down.

22:02.710 --> 22:04.720
There is no point in developing 
your mental fortitude

22:04.720 --> 22:07.120
only for it to be disturbed again.

22:07.120 --> 22:11.470
What you require right now is a palpable 
sense of the danger you are in.

22:14.930 --> 22:19.070
You must score in the school's 
top ten on your next test.

22:19.070 --> 22:23.810
If you are unable to do that, 
I will send you straight back to Tokyo!
